    "lawCode": "Amd §§243, 324 & 422, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3828\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nto amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation\nto free and reduced fee\npasses, cards and badges\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill authorize and encourage racetracks to conduct\npromotional campaigns to increase attendance at New York's\nthoroughbred and harness race tracks. This is being done by\nauthorizing such race tracks to expand the number of persons that are\nqualified to obtain a free or reduced fee pass, card or badge to\nenter a race track, at the discretion of such track. Giving\nracetracks more latitude to develop and implement promotional\ncampaigns geared to the general public may help such tracks to\nincrease attendance at such facilities.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Racing & Wagering Law section 243 to expand the\nnumber of persons that are qualified to obtain a free or reduced fee\npass, card or badge to enter a thoroughbred race track to include any\nother person or guest that is deemed appropriate by the operator of\nsuch thoroughbred race track or as part of promotional campaign open\nto the general public or a segment of the general public.\n\nSection 2: Amends Racing & Wagering Law section 324 to expand the\nnumber of persons that are qualified to obtain a free or reduced fee\npass, card or badge to enter a harness race track to include any\nother person or guest that is deemed appropriate by the operator of\nsuch harness race track. In addition, free or reduced fee passes may\nbe issued to the general public in connection with any track\nsponsored promotional campaign or marketing program to increase live\nrace attendance.\n\nSection 3: Amends Racing & wagering Law section 422 to expand the\nnumber of persons that are qualified to obtain a free or reduced fee\npass, card or badge to enter a quarter horse race track to include\nany other person or guest that is deemed appropriate by the operator\nof such quarter horse race track. Also, free or reduced fee passes\nmay be issued to the general public to increase public participation\nat such quarter horse events.\n\nSection 4: Effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nUnder current law, only a select group of public officers and\nemployees engaged in the regulation of racing events and employees of\nthe racing industry that are conducting race meets are allowed to be\nawarded free passes, cards or badges to enter a horse race track.\n\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, horse owners and racing industry regulators may\nobtain free passes to enter into a racetrack, however members of the\nhorse owner's family and friends are precluded from receiving such\npasses. Attendance at horse racing events has been in a steady\ndecline for the past thirty years.\nThis had lead to reduced betting handle for the racetrack and a less\nthan exciting experience for the racing fan. This is an outdated law\nthat needs to be revised.\n\nThis measure will allow horse race track operators to issue more free\nor reduced fee passes to promote attendance of individuals at live\nhorse racing events. Allowing the issuance of more free passes will\nnot only increase attendance and the excitement of those horse racing\nevents, it may encourage an increase in betting handle at such racing\nfacilities and the patronage of restaurants located at such tracks.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis bill should increase attendance at live horse racing events,\nconsequently, it may increase the betting handle and the taxes\ncollected on such handle.\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nEncouraging more attendance at live horse racing events and the\nprofits generated by such events will enhance a racing facility's\nability to pay local property and use taxes.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on the 180th day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n\n",
